CAT = "cparegStructure"; SEG = "STR"
Q = [
("Partners in a general partnership are liable for partnership debts:",
 "Personally, jointly and severally", ["Only up to their investment", "Only for debts they signed", "Only if the veil is pierced"],
 "Under the Revised Uniform Partnership Act, partners are jointly and severally liable for partnership obligations, though a creditor generally pursues partnership assets first."),
("In a limited partnership, which partner has unlimited personal liability for its debts?",
 "Each general partner", ["Each limited partner", "The largest investor", "The newest partner"],
 "A limited partnership needs at least one general partner, who is personally liable. Limited partners risk only their investment."),
("Under the Revised Model Business Corporation Act, a corporation comes into existence when:",
 "Its articles are filed", ["Its bylaws are adopted", "Its first shares are issued", "Its directors first meet"],
 "Corporate existence begins when the articles of incorporation are filed with the secretary of state. Bylaws and the organizational meeting follow."),
("A promoter signs a lease for a corporation not yet formed. After it is formed, the corporation adopts the lease. The promoter is:",
 "Liable until a novation", ["Released by the adoption", "Liable for one month only", "Never liable on the lease"],
 "A promoter stays personally liable on a pre-incorporation contract even after the corporation adopts it. Only a novation, in which the other party releases the promoter, ends that liability."),
("A director makes an informed, good-faith decision that later loses the company money. Under the business judgment rule, the director is:",
 "Not personally liable", ["Liable for the full loss", "Liable for half the loss", "Liable if shareholders vote so"],
 "The business judgment rule protects directors who act in good faith, with reasonable care and in the corporation's best interest, even if the decision turns out badly."),
("Who has authority to declare a cash dividend in a corporation?",
 "The board of directors", ["The majority shareholders", "The chief executive", "The corporate treasurer"],
 "Declaring dividends is a board decision. Once declared, a cash dividend becomes a debt the corporation owes to its shareholders."),
("A shareholder sues the directors for harm done to the corporation. Any recovery generally goes to:",
 "The corporation", ["The suing shareholder", "All shareholders pro rata", "The directors' insurer"],
 "In a derivative suit the shareholder sues on the corporation's behalf, so recovery belongs to the corporation. The shareholder may recover litigation costs."),
("A partner transfers her transferable interest in a general partnership to a creditor. The creditor receives:",
 "Her share of distributions", ["Her right to manage", "Her vote on new partners", "Full partner status"],
 "A transferee of a partner's transferable interest gets only the right to that partner's distributions. Management and voting rights stay with the partner."),
]
